ISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular portion of tan skin with an eccentric unremarkable nipple and a 5 0cm well healed  linear scar running from superior to inferior  Connected to this ellipse of skin is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm strip of tan skin along the inferior aspect that contains a 13 5cm linear  well healed scar  There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the lateral aspect  Within the parenchyma there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm poorly circumscribed white firm mass with an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm extension  The mass is less than 0 1cm from the deep margin  and 0 8cm from the anterior superior margin  1 5cm medial to this mass  there is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm hard firm white mass that is 1 0cm from the deep margin and 2 0cm from the closest anterior superior margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is notable for several small  discrete firm white nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 9cm  these are scattered throughout the parenchyma