s of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a specimen in three parts  Labeled  Right breast mass  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm breast tissue  with irregular hard areas throughout the specimen  which is entirely submitted in A J and BB GG  Labeled  Right breast mass  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast tissue with multiple pinpoint yellow areas throughout the specimen  with some harder areas  No mass is identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K   V  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of breast tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hard nodular area  The specimen is submitted entirely in W   AA  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX 1 and 2  BREAST  RIGHT   1 AND  2   BIOPSIES  FIRM  POTENTIALLY ABNORMAL AREAS IN BOTH SPECIMENS  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DX  3  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  FEW VERY SMALL  FIRM AREAS  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCE