rmined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen inked and sectioned to reveal diffuse fibroelastic white tissue  There are two firm nodules of white gray granular gritty tissue abutting the inked margin  Each of these nodules are a few millimeters apart measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm respectively  One section containing both nodules is frozen as FX 1  now in A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in B F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  silicone implant right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm of thin membraned  yellow gelatinous foreign body consistent with a silicone implant  The specimen is for gross only  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  silicone implant left  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm gelatinous thin membraned  foreign body consistent with a silicon implant  The specimen is for gross diagnosis only  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional right breast tissue  is a large fragment of tan yellow focally white fibrofatty piece of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  Also received in the same jar is a smaller tan white fibrofatty fragment measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  In addition  in the same jar there is a tan white smooth  piece of fibrous soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The larger fragment is serially sectioned to reveal tan white firm fibrous parenchyma with focal areas of yellow lobated fat  The specimen is submitted in entirety in G K  The smaller fragment is bivalved to reveal a tan white fibrous cut surface  This small fragment as well as the serially sectioned  thin membranous piece are submitted entirely in L M  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  IMPLANT  RIGHT BREAST  PART C  IMPLANT  LEFT BREAST  PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 98 at 10 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 MAY 98 at 18 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft  tan cores of tissue  which are submitted in toto in Cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Not_reported.
